            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>International Relations</strong><br>\nSolomon's era was marked by peace and he formed alliances through marriage, taking many wives from neighboring countries. These alliances helped to stabilize Israel's position in the region and increased trade and cultural exchange.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Expansions</strong><br>\nUnder Solomon, Israel's economy flourished. He conducted trade with distant lands, including Arabia and Africa. He was renowned for his extensive building projects, which required massive resources and labor, boosting the local economy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Administration of Israel</strong><br>\nSolomon's government was large and complex. He divided the kingdom into districts, appointing officials to collect taxes to fund his projects and policies. This centralized bureaucracy helped maintain order and support the ambitious building and economic programs.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
