          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Solomon's Writings</strong><br>\nSolomon is credited with composing many works, including Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and the Song of Solomon. These texts are considered wisdom literature and offer insight into his philosophical and spiritual beliefs.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Religious Beliefs and Practices</strong><br>\nThough Solomon initially followed the religious practices of Israel, his many marriages to foreign women led him to introduce and tolerate their diverse pagan worship, which eventually displeased many in the kingdom.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Solomon's Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter Solomon's death, his actions, especially his heavy taxation and forced labor practices, led to the division of his kingdom. Yet, his legacy of wisdom and the opulence of his reign have become proverbial, cementing his place as one of Israel's most famous and controversial kings.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
